 "_doc": "The undercroft (design/places/ring1-places-and-fights-spec.md \u00a74.3; build item N-7.1.3): the cistern-drain under the city's Sunken Square, four rooms: the drain stair, the long channel (knee-deep water three cells wide), the sluice room (its wheel drains the channel: water rects drained while the life flag `channel_dry` is set) and the grate hall. Same keys as the halls. exits may carry `opened_by`, a soul memory: the exit only works once you know it. shortcuts: a way that opens for good (kept across lives, as the soul memory `know`): the drain grate opens when its `weight` prop (the counterweight crate) is shoved into its rect, or lightning at `grade` charges the chain's rail cell at `winch`. Generated by the scratchpad's undercroft_gen.py; check it with tools/map_preview.gd.",
